[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127308,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nuchal-type fibroma is a benign fibroblastic tumour characterized by abundant thick collagen bundles, most commonly arising in the posterior neck.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127309,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "<p>8810/0 Nuchal-type fibroma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-06-30T10:28:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127310,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH0XH6 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Nuchal fibroma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127311,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> nuchal fibroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> collagenosis nuchae.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127312,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127313,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common site is the posterior neck {9921988}, but other sites can be involved. Nuchal-type fibroma most often involves the subcutaneous soft tissue, sometimes with dermal and skeletal muscle involvement.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127314,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients typically present with a long history of a solitary, superficial to deep, painless swelling; rarely, lesions can be multiple {7872429; 21950671; 9921988}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127315,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nuchal-type fibroma has a male predilection and a peak incidence between the third and fifth decades of life.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127316,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is an association with diabetes; in one series, 11&nbsp;of 25&nbsp;patients with nuchal-type fibroma (44%) also had diabetes {9921988}. Some tumours are associated with Gardner syndrome {9921988}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127317,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A few tested cases were found to have <em>APC</em> mutations. One case had a mutation in <em>MUTYH</em>, which encodes a base excision repair protein and has also been implicated in familial adenomatous polyposis {21752055}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127318,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nuchal-type fibromas are firm, poorly circumscribed masses, 10&ndash;80&nbsp;mm in size, with a white cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127319,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nuchal-type fibromas are poorly circumscribed, hypocellular, and characterized by thick collagen fibres and small fibroblasts. Entrapped islands of fat, skeletal muscle, and nerves with traumatic neuroma&ndash;like changes can be seen. This feature is usually absent from Gardner fibroma, which is often otherwise indistinguishable from nuchal-type fibroma. Elastic fibres and small blood vessels are present between the collagen fibres.</p>\r\n<h6>Immunohistochemistry</h6>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry is not specific; the tumours are negative for desmin, actin, S100, and EMA {7872429; 9921988}. There may be nuclear expression of &beta;-catenin.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes desmoid-type fibromatosis and Gardner fibroma (which may be related).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127320,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127321,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Some cases may have mutations in <em>APC</em> or <em>MUTYH</em>; however, mutation analyses are usually unnecessary for the diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127322,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> poorly circumscribed hypocellular tumours with small fibroblasts and thick collagen fibres; entrapped fat and nerves.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127323,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127324,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 383,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nuchal-type fibroma is benign. Excision is curative and local recurrence is rare {7872429; 9921988}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:37:36"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]